WEBVTT

00:00:09.176 --> 00:00:13.180
I can't take it anymore!
They've been at it for hours!

00:00:14.723 --> 00:00:16.225
Give it a rest, you two!

00:00:21.063 --> 00:00:22.272
Sorry!

00:00:58.367 --> 00:00:59.868
Good morning, class.

00:00:59.952 --> 00:01:03.205
I trust you've all prepared
for today's final exam.

00:01:03.288 --> 00:01:07.501
Uh, excuse me. I missed a few lectures.
Uh, what subject is this?

00:01:07.584 --> 00:01:10.337
Ancient Egyptian algebra.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:12.089
What a nightmare!

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:16.134
Mr. Fry, are those your underpants?

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:21.390
Young man, I think it's time

00:01:21.473 --> 00:01:24.893
you learned a lesson
about Lightspeed brand briefs.

00:01:24.977 --> 00:01:27.896
Lightspeed fits
today's active lifestyle

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:29.481
whether you're on the job...

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:31.650
Or having fun.

00:01:32.787 --> 00:01:34.205
Lightspeed briefs...

00:01:34.269 --> 00:01:36.897
Style and comfort
for the discriminating crotch.

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:39.483
Oh! What a weird dream.

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:41.652
I'll never get back to sleep.

00:01:48.617 --> 00:01:51.828
So, you're telling me they broadcast
commercials into people's dreams?

00:01:51.912 --> 00:01:54.122
- Of course.
- But how is that possible?

00:01:54.206 --> 00:01:55.707
It's very simple.

00:01:55.791 --> 00:02:00.003
The ad gets into your brain
just like this liquid gets into this egg.

00:02:01.338 --> 00:02:05.676
Although, in reality,
it's not liquid, but gamma radiation.

00:02:05.759 --> 00:02:08.095
That's awful. It's like brainwashing.

00:02:08.178 --> 00:02:10.389
Didn't you have ads in the 20th century?

00:02:10.472 --> 00:02:12.724
Well, sure, but not in our dreams.

00:02:12.808 --> 00:02:14.810
Only on TV and radio...

00:02:14.893 --> 00:02:16.144
And in magazines...

00:02:16.228 --> 00:02:17.312
And movies...

00:02:17.396 --> 00:02:18.480
And at ball games...

00:02:18.564 --> 00:02:22.317
And on buses and milk cartons
and T-shirts and bananas

00:02:22.401 --> 00:02:23.694
and written on the sky,

00:02:23.777 --> 00:02:24.987
but not in dreams.

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:26.446
No, sirree.

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:30.409
Quit squawking, fleshwad.
Nobody's forcing you to buy anything.

00:02:30.492 --> 00:02:32.995
Yeah. I mean,
we all had commercials in our dreams,

00:02:33.078 --> 00:02:37.165
but you don't see us running off to buy
brand-name merchandise at low, low prices.

00:02:52.556 --> 00:02:56.184
Hi. Care to sample the latest fragrance
from Calvin Clone?

00:02:56.268 --> 00:02:57.311
No, thanks.

00:02:59.062 --> 00:03:00.063
And you, sir?

00:03:00.147 --> 00:03:01.857
No, thanks. I...

00:03:07.029 --> 00:03:09.072
What a lovely face.

00:03:09.156 --> 00:03:13.035
We just need to draw attention
away from the eye area.

00:03:21.293 --> 00:03:22.294
Cool.

00:03:24.171 --> 00:03:26.131
Can I try these on before I buy them?

00:03:26.214 --> 00:03:28.717
I'm afraid
I can't let you open the package,

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:31.136
but you can try on the demo pair.

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:36.767
Ooh.

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:38.518
Ho-ho-ho.

00:03:58.205 --> 00:04:00.207
Hey, Bender. Great new sweater.

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:03.585
Uh, "new"? What sweater?
I came in with it!

00:04:03.669 --> 00:04:05.128
I don't know you people.

00:04:10.175 --> 00:04:11.510
$30, please.

00:04:11.593 --> 00:04:14.137
$30? I can't afford that.

00:04:14.221 --> 00:04:15.847
Unless...

00:04:15.931 --> 00:04:16.974
Do you take Visa?

00:04:17.057 --> 00:04:19.226
Visa hasn't existed for 500 years.

00:04:19.309 --> 00:04:21.520
- American Express?
- 600 years.

00:04:21.603 --> 00:04:24.481
- Discover card?
- Mm, sorry, we don't take Discover.

00:04:24.565 --> 00:04:28.110
Hey... You're springing for Lightspeeds?
Pretty ritzy.

00:04:28.193 --> 00:04:31.029
No, I can't afford them. Being poor sucks.

00:04:31.113 --> 00:04:35.075
What kind of world is this where they
advertise things not everybody can afford?

00:04:35.158 --> 00:04:36.743
Quiet. There's an ad coming on.

00:04:38.203 --> 00:04:39.413
Hello, shoppers.

00:04:39.496 --> 00:04:40.956
It's me, Mom.

00:04:41.039 --> 00:04:44.126
- Hey, who's the rocker jockey?
- Guh! It's Mom,

00:04:44.209 --> 00:04:46.461
the world's most huggable industrialist.

00:04:46.545 --> 00:04:48.213
Call me old-fashioned,

00:04:48.297 --> 00:04:51.842
but when my robot starts to squeak
like an old screen door,

00:04:51.925 --> 00:04:56.597
well, that's when I reach for a can
of Mom's Old-Fashioned Robot Oil.

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:57.973
Ooh, tasty.

00:04:58.056 --> 00:05:04.438
And remember, Mom's Oil is made with
10% more love than the next leading brand.

00:05:04.521 --> 00:05:07.774
"Mom," "love" and "screen door"
are registered trademarks of Momcorp.

00:05:09.568 --> 00:05:12.529
Hey, Bender, sounds like
you can use a little of that oil.

00:05:13.155 --> 00:05:14.156
Um...

00:05:16.283 --> 00:05:17.326
I'm boned.

00:05:17.409 --> 00:05:18.452
Freeze, scuzzbot!

00:05:18.535 --> 00:05:22.205
Uh, there's obviously been
some sort of a mistake here.

00:05:24.374 --> 00:05:25.584
I'm sure there's...

00:05:27.294 --> 00:05:30.088
I say, I'm sure there's...

00:05:31.256 --> 00:05:34.051
That is, I'm sure there's...

00:05:34.134 --> 00:05:35.594
A very...

00:05:35.677 --> 00:05:36.887
Reasonable...

00:05:44.811 --> 00:05:47.272
Do we have enough money
to pay Bender's fine?

00:05:47.356 --> 00:05:50.567
Seventy-eight, 79, 79.50.

00:05:50.651 --> 00:05:52.986
Crud. We're 50 cents short.

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:55.822
I'd love to chip in,
but Bender stole my wallet.

00:05:57.199 --> 00:05:58.784
Hey, that's my old bank.

00:05:58.867 --> 00:06:00.827
Maybe my account's still open.

00:06:05.958 --> 00:06:08.460
Hmm. We don't seem
to have your retina scan,

00:06:08.543 --> 00:06:11.255
your fingerprint
or your colonic map on file.

00:06:11.338 --> 00:06:14.383
Yeah, well, I did open the account
over a thousand years ago.

00:06:14.466 --> 00:06:15.801
What about my ATM card?

00:06:16.468 --> 00:06:19.012
Do you still remember
your pin number?

00:06:19.096 --> 00:06:21.807
Sure. It's the price
of a cheese pizza and a large soda

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:24.101
back where I used to work...
Pinucci's Pizza.

00:06:24.935 --> 00:06:28.230
Okay. You had a balance of 93 cents.

00:06:28.313 --> 00:06:29.314
All right.

00:06:29.398 --> 00:06:32.109
And at an average
of two and a quarter percent interest

00:06:32.192 --> 00:06:34.736
over a period of 1,000 years,
that comes to...

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:36.530
$4.3 billion.

00:06:46.456 --> 00:06:47.833
- To Fry.
- Cheers!

00:06:55.966 --> 00:06:59.469
I know Fry's rich, but do we really
have to wear these top hats?

00:06:59.553 --> 00:07:02.723
Maybe you don't understand
just how rich he is.

00:07:02.806 --> 00:07:05.475
In fact,
I think I better put on a monocle.

00:07:32.669 --> 00:07:34.129
Pizza dinner on me.

00:07:35.589 --> 00:07:38.675
Just keep the tab under $50 million.

00:07:38.759 --> 00:07:42.638
Yo. I haven't got all day.
What kind of pizza yous guys want?

00:07:42.721 --> 00:07:46.225
Uh, yeah, we'll have, uh,
one with everything but anchovies

00:07:46.308 --> 00:07:48.727
and, uh,
one with my all-time favorite topping...

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:49.853
Anchovies.

00:07:49.937 --> 00:07:51.396
Invalid selection.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:53.440
Yo,
what are you talking about?

00:07:53.523 --> 00:07:56.068
Anchovies. You know,
those little headless fish?

00:07:56.151 --> 00:07:57.569
Does not compute.

00:07:57.653 --> 00:07:58.904
Does not compute.

00:08:01.531 --> 00:08:06.036
I'm sorry, Fry, but the anchovy
has been extinct since the 2200s.

00:08:06.119 --> 00:08:09.331
- What?
- Oh, my, yes, fished to death...

00:08:09.414 --> 00:08:13.210
Just about the time your people
arrived on Earth, wasn't it, Zoidberg?

00:08:13.293 --> 00:08:14.920
I'm not on trial here.

00:08:15.003 --> 00:08:17.005
So none of you has ever had anchovies?

00:08:17.089 --> 00:08:19.508
Oh, man,
you don't know what you're missing.

00:08:19.591 --> 00:08:22.761
They were all salty and oily,
and they melted in your mouth...

00:08:22.844 --> 00:08:26.682
Stop! Stop! I admit it.
My people ate them all.

00:08:26.765 --> 00:08:30.561
We kept saying, "one more can't hurt,"
and then they were gone.

00:08:30.644 --> 00:08:32.020
We're sorry!

00:08:32.104 --> 00:08:35.983
I just wish I could have
showed you guys how great they were.

00:08:36.066 --> 00:08:38.151
I may be rich, but I still can't buy back

00:08:38.235 --> 00:08:40.404
all the things I miss
from the 20th century.

00:08:40.487 --> 00:08:43.448
Maybe you're forgetting
just how rich you are.

00:08:44.199 --> 00:08:45.826
Huh? Huh?

00:08:49.997 --> 00:08:50.998
Yeah!

00:08:54.501 --> 00:08:55.711
So, what do you think?

00:08:55.794 --> 00:08:58.630
I know you spent a lot of money
on this place, Fry,

00:08:58.714 --> 00:09:00.132
but it's awfully primitive.

00:09:00.591 --> 00:09:03.051
The floors are made of such hard wood.

00:09:03.135 --> 00:09:07.097
Hey, get a load of this
pathetic 20th-century TV.

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:08.265
What's wrong with it?

00:09:08.348 --> 00:09:10.893
Well, aside from causing eye cancer,

00:09:10.976 --> 00:09:13.812
these things had a lousy,
low-definition picture.

00:09:13.896 --> 00:09:14.897
That's true.

00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:18.275
On a TV like this, I bet you couldn't even
make out my obscene tattoo.

00:09:18.358 --> 00:09:20.611
That's cute.

00:09:24.114 --> 00:09:25.115
Sold!

00:09:25.198 --> 00:09:26.199
Yes!

00:09:26.283 --> 00:09:27.451
I just don't get it.

00:09:27.534 --> 00:09:29.411
Who was this Ted Danson

00:09:29.494 --> 00:09:32.205
and why would you pay $10,000
for his skeleton?

00:09:32.289 --> 00:09:33.999
I have an idea for a sitcom.

00:09:34.082 --> 00:09:35.876
Ah, leave him alone, Leela.

00:09:35.959 --> 00:09:38.170
So he's going
a little wacko with his money.

00:09:38.253 --> 00:09:39.254
That's okay.

00:09:39.338 --> 00:09:40.547
You're just saying that

00:09:40.631 --> 00:09:42.883
'cause he bought you
that antique robot toy.

00:09:42.966 --> 00:09:45.427
Yeah.

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:47.221
It is cute.

00:09:48.639 --> 00:09:51.934
Now, our final item, this unopened can

00:09:52.017 --> 00:09:56.647
of Angry Norwegian brand anchovies,
circa 1997.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:58.148
Anchovies?

00:09:58.232 --> 00:10:02.402
The last known can in existence,
guaranteed fresh and edible.

00:10:02.486 --> 00:10:04.321
Do I hear $10,000?

00:10:04.404 --> 00:10:05.530
$15,000.

00:10:05.614 --> 00:10:07.199
Twenty.

00:10:07.282 --> 00:10:09.493
Thirty. No, 40.

00:10:09.576 --> 00:10:11.954
$50,000.

00:10:12.996 --> 00:10:15.415
Are you crazy? It's a can of old fish.

00:10:15.499 --> 00:10:17.459
Don't tell me how to spend my money.

00:10:17.542 --> 00:10:19.795
Fifty, going once, twice...

00:10:19.878 --> 00:10:21.505
$75,000.

00:10:24.007 --> 00:10:25.801
Oh, my God. It's Mom.

00:10:25.884 --> 00:10:28.053
I've never seen her in person before.

00:10:28.136 --> 00:10:29.805
$100,000.

00:10:32.349 --> 00:10:34.268
Fry, you can't bid against Mom.

00:10:34.351 --> 00:10:37.104
She's the richest,
most powerful person in the world.

00:10:37.187 --> 00:10:38.772
And she's so adorable.

00:10:38.855 --> 00:10:42.609
Well, I suppose I could go as high as...

00:10:42.693 --> 00:10:43.735
$300,000.

00:10:43.819 --> 00:10:46.530
- Five hundred.
- Oh, mercy me. A million.

00:10:46.613 --> 00:10:47.482
- Two.
- Six.

00:10:47.507 --> 00:10:48.508
Fourteen.

00:10:48.533 --> 00:10:52.010
I can see the nice young man
really wants those little fish.

00:10:52.035 --> 00:10:54.413
Nevertheless, I'll bid $23 million.

00:10:54.496 --> 00:10:56.707
One jillion dollars.

00:10:57.958 --> 00:10:59.835
Sir, that's not a number.

00:11:01.461 --> 00:11:04.506
Oh. In that case... $50 million.

00:11:05.924 --> 00:11:10.220
Well, boys, your old mother knows
when she's been beat.

00:11:10.304 --> 00:11:13.891
You win, young man.
I tip my bonnet to you.

00:11:13.974 --> 00:11:16.393
Oh, isn't she adorable?

00:11:16.476 --> 00:11:18.604
What a class act. Sold!

00:11:18.687 --> 00:11:21.648
To the gentleman who bought
every item In today's auction.

00:11:29.072 --> 00:11:32.284
Now for some good old 20th-century TV.

00:11:34.369 --> 00:11:35.662
Ah.

00:11:35.746 --> 00:11:37.456
Do you remember a time

00:11:37.539 --> 00:11:40.334
when chocolate chip cookies
came fresh from the oven?

00:11:40.417 --> 00:11:41.919
Petridge Farm remembers.

00:11:42.002 --> 00:11:43.378
Oh, those were the days.

00:11:43.462 --> 00:11:46.173
Do you remember a time
when women couldn't vote

00:11:46.256 --> 00:11:48.884
and certain folk
weren't allowed on golf courses?

00:11:48.967 --> 00:11:50.719
Petridge Farm remembers.

00:11:51.929 --> 00:11:54.473
- Fry, are you there?
- Huh?

00:11:56.391 --> 00:11:59.686
You haven't been to work in three days.
What have you been doing?

00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:01.230
I've been sitting right here.

00:12:01.313 --> 00:12:04.942
I picked up my life exactly where
I left off a thousand years ago.

00:12:05.025 --> 00:12:09.446
Now, if you'll excuse me, it's 8:00.
Time to get busy.

00:12:10.781 --> 00:12:13.909
I like big butts and I cannot lie
You other brothers can't deny

00:12:15.118 --> 00:12:17.913
You can't just sit here in the dark
listening to classical music.

00:12:17.996 --> 00:12:21.333
I could if you hadn't turned on the lights
and shut off the stereo.

00:12:21.416 --> 00:12:23.919
Fry, this isn't healthy.
You're living in the past.

00:12:24.002 --> 00:12:26.338
I'm rich. I can live whenever I want.

00:12:26.421 --> 00:12:29.800
But we're your friends,
and we live here in the year 3000.

00:12:29.883 --> 00:12:30.884
Yeah.

00:12:30.968 --> 00:12:33.637
Now, are you going to come
to the squid fights with us

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:36.807
or sit here wallowing
in your prehistoric junk?

00:12:36.890 --> 00:12:38.058
Junk?

00:12:38.141 --> 00:12:39.810
Maybe you can't understand this,

00:12:39.893 --> 00:12:42.396
but I finally found
what I need to be happy,

00:12:42.479 --> 00:12:44.731
and it's not friends, it's things.

00:12:44.815 --> 00:12:46.191
I'm a thing.

00:12:46.275 --> 00:12:47.943
Just leave me alone.

00:12:50.529 --> 00:12:51.655
Fry, please.

00:12:52.489 --> 00:12:55.075
My ponytail's caught in the door.

00:12:55.158 --> 00:12:56.326
I don't need them.

00:12:56.410 --> 00:13:00.664
Not when I have my antique videos,
my bucket of fossilized KFC

00:13:00.747 --> 00:13:03.458
and $50 million worth of anchovies.

00:13:07.296 --> 00:13:09.548
Mercy me, what a day.

00:13:09.631 --> 00:13:12.175
Could you shut the door, Igner, dear?

00:13:12.259 --> 00:13:14.595
I think I feel a draft coming on.

00:13:18.265 --> 00:13:20.475
Holy crap, that bastard's itchy.

00:13:21.059 --> 00:13:22.311
Walt, cream soda.

00:13:22.394 --> 00:13:23.770
Right away, Mother.

00:13:23.854 --> 00:13:25.856
Larry, get your mother a cream soda.

00:13:25.939 --> 00:13:27.149
But Mom said...

00:13:27.232 --> 00:13:28.567
You heard me.

00:13:37.284 --> 00:13:38.368
What's wrong, Mommy?

00:13:38.452 --> 00:13:40.787
It's those damned anchovies.

00:13:40.871 --> 00:13:43.290
That dirtbag Fry must know their secret

00:13:43.373 --> 00:13:46.418
and I won't rest
until I get my hands on them.

00:13:46.501 --> 00:13:49.671
No one messes with Mom.

00:13:59.514 --> 00:14:00.599
Quiet, you.

00:14:06.021 --> 00:14:09.233
As you boys know,
one of the cornerstones of my empire

00:14:09.316 --> 00:14:11.652
is Mom's Old-Fashioned Robot Oil.

00:14:11.735 --> 00:14:14.905
Think of it, ten billion robots,

00:14:14.988 --> 00:14:18.533
each one needing an oil change
every 3,000 miles.

00:14:18.617 --> 00:14:22.162
You don't have to do the math
to know that's a buttload of oil.

00:14:22.246 --> 00:14:23.580
Can I wear your fat suit?

00:14:23.664 --> 00:14:25.123
No, Igner, put that down!

00:14:25.207 --> 00:14:26.250
Ohh.

00:14:26.333 --> 00:14:28.543
What does this have to do
with the anchovies?

00:14:28.627 --> 00:14:32.172
I'm getting to the freaking anchovies.

00:14:33.966 --> 00:14:38.470
A single drop of the anchovy's natural oil
would lubricate ten robots permanently.

00:14:38.554 --> 00:14:40.097
Wow. It's a shame they went extinct.

00:14:40.180 --> 00:14:42.099
No, it isn't! Shut your filthy clam!

00:14:43.058 --> 00:14:44.851
Thank you, Walt.

00:14:44.935 --> 00:14:49.898
If anyone ever got hold of anchovy DNA,
they could chop out the oil-making gene,

00:14:49.982 --> 00:14:52.609
stick it in a bunch of third world kids
and bam!

00:14:52.693 --> 00:14:54.444
Cheap, effective robot oil.

00:14:54.528 --> 00:14:57.447
Enough to put dear old Mom
out of business.

00:14:57.531 --> 00:15:03.203
My God, this Mr. Fry
must be a mastermind of the highest order.

00:15:08.375 --> 00:15:10.752
Esther, you ugly.

00:15:10.836 --> 00:15:12.296
We have only one option.

00:15:12.379 --> 00:15:14.548
We'll have to bankrupt Mr. Fry

00:15:14.631 --> 00:15:17.134
so he'll be forced
to sell the anchovies to us.

00:15:17.217 --> 00:15:20.304
Mother, you are one clever old scag.

00:15:20.387 --> 00:15:21.722
And don't you forget it.

00:15:21.805 --> 00:15:24.224
But how are we supposed to get
Fry's money out of the bank?

00:15:24.308 --> 00:15:27.144
That part will be easy,
thanks to the nice people

00:15:27.227 --> 00:15:29.855
at Mom's Old-Fashioned
Video Surveillance unit.

00:15:31.481 --> 00:15:32.941
Do you still remember your pin number?

00:15:33.025 --> 00:15:35.986
Sure. It's the price
of a cheese pizza and a large soda

00:15:36.069 --> 00:15:38.280
back where I used to work...
Pinucci's Pizza.

00:15:40.240 --> 00:15:42.409
It's the price of a cheese pizza
and a large soda.

00:15:42.492 --> 00:15:44.745
You know what needs to be done.

00:15:45.331 --> 00:15:45.829
What?

00:15:45.913 --> 00:15:48.832
Get his pin number, you idiots!

00:15:48.916 --> 00:15:53.670
Now I'm off to some charity BS
for knocked-up teenage sluts.

00:15:57.132 --> 00:16:00.719
Mr. Fry,
it's those three plumbers you called for.

00:16:00.802 --> 00:16:02.888
We're here to tighten your drains.

00:16:02.971 --> 00:16:04.223
Ow!

00:16:06.934 --> 00:16:08.477
I didn't order any...

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:10.270
Quick! Give him the tranquilizer.

00:16:13.690 --> 00:16:15.692
That's a good boy.

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:22.741
Wake up, Mr. Fry.

00:16:22.824 --> 00:16:24.576
Where am I?

00:16:24.660 --> 00:16:28.372
You're in the good old year 2000
working here at Pinucci's Pizza.

00:16:28.455 --> 00:16:30.415
You fell asleep on the job.

00:16:30.499 --> 00:16:34.002
Well, that sounds like me,
but I thought I got frozen.

00:16:34.086 --> 00:16:35.587
Wasn't I in the future?

00:16:35.671 --> 00:16:39.216
No, you only "dreamed"
you were in the year 3000.

00:16:39.299 --> 00:16:40.926
So I'm really back?

00:16:41.009 --> 00:16:43.637
Well, that's exactly what I wanted,
I guess.

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:44.763
Who are you?

00:16:44.846 --> 00:16:46.056
I'm Mr. Pinucci.

00:16:46.139 --> 00:16:47.182
You are?

00:16:47.266 --> 00:16:49.560
Did-did you grow a mustache
since last night?

00:16:49.643 --> 00:16:52.938
No. Now, go work the currency register.

00:16:53.021 --> 00:16:55.440
I think I hear a customer coming.

00:16:55.524 --> 00:16:58.277
I said,
"I think I hear a customer coming."

00:16:59.987 --> 00:17:03.115
Oh, hurry up, please.
I want to get back to the head museum.

00:17:03.198 --> 00:17:05.617
Don't worry, Miss Anderson.
This won't take long.

00:17:05.701 --> 00:17:08.954
Now, your motivation is,
you're back in the year 2000

00:17:09.037 --> 00:17:12.499
and your head's still on your body
and you want a cheese pizza.

00:17:16.003 --> 00:17:17.838
Okay, but I'm only doing this

00:17:17.921 --> 00:17:20.507
so people will take my head seriously
as an actress.

00:17:21.466 --> 00:17:23.093
Hey, look... Anchovies.

00:17:23.176 --> 00:17:26.138
Of course. They're not extinct yet.

00:17:26.221 --> 00:17:30.642
And if you need further proof
that this is really a thousand years ago,

00:17:30.726 --> 00:17:34.229
well, here's contemporary actress
Pamela Anderson.

00:17:35.981 --> 00:17:36.982
Ooh.

00:17:38.275 --> 00:17:39.568
Hello, Fry.

00:17:39.651 --> 00:17:41.528
The Movie?

00:17:41.612 --> 00:17:42.696
Uh...

00:17:42.779 --> 00:17:46.158
It was the first movie
to be shot entirely in slow motion.

00:17:46.241 --> 00:17:48.118
It hasn't been made yet.

00:17:48.201 --> 00:17:49.786
Then he doesn't know
I won the Oscar?

00:17:49.870 --> 00:17:51.663
- Nope.
- Crap!

00:17:51.747 --> 00:17:54.124
Wait. You're Pamela Anderson.

00:17:54.207 --> 00:17:56.293
Cool. What can I get you?

00:17:56.626 --> 00:17:59.713
Oh, I'll have a cheese pizza
and a large...

00:17:59.738 --> 00:18:01.949
Uh... Line?

00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:04.092
- Soda.
- Oh, right.

00:18:04.176 --> 00:18:06.803
Cheese pizza
and a large soda.

00:18:06.887 --> 00:18:09.431
Uh, cheese and a...

00:18:09.514 --> 00:18:10.515
That was quick.

00:18:10.599 --> 00:18:12.642
So, what do I owe you?

00:18:13.685 --> 00:18:15.353
$10.77...

00:18:15.437 --> 00:18:16.771
Same as my pin number.

00:18:24.579 --> 00:18:26.873
Hey, you don't get to laugh.

00:18:30.752 --> 00:18:32.129
Thanks a billion.

00:18:33.964 --> 00:18:36.174
More like 4.3 billion.

00:18:37.217 --> 00:18:38.844
- Oh!
- Ow!

00:18:49.771 --> 00:18:52.357
Uh, I had a nightmare
I was in the year 2000

00:18:52.441 --> 00:18:54.192
and you guys never existed.

00:18:54.276 --> 00:18:56.820
I'm so glad I'm awake now
and you're really here.

00:18:56.903 --> 00:18:58.530
Since when do you care about us?

00:18:58.614 --> 00:19:01.283
We thought you only cared about
cans of anchovies

00:19:01.366 --> 00:19:03.368
and stuffy old songs about the buttocks.

00:19:03.452 --> 00:19:05.203
No, that's not true.

00:19:05.287 --> 00:19:06.997
Goodbye.

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:10.000
Whee!

00:19:10.083 --> 00:19:13.003
This dream brought to you
by Lightspeed briefs.

00:19:13.086 --> 00:19:14.921
Bender, Leela...

00:19:15.005 --> 00:19:16.131
Don't leave me.

00:19:17.174 --> 00:19:20.052
Wait a minute.
Hey, hey, buddy, what year is this?

00:19:20.135 --> 00:19:22.346
Uh... 3000.

00:19:22.429 --> 00:19:23.472
3000?

00:19:23.555 --> 00:19:28.018
Yes! I'm still in the future!
Life is wonderful!

00:19:28.101 --> 00:19:30.062
Wait. What are you doing with my stuff?

00:19:30.145 --> 00:19:33.732
Uh, check bounced.
We're taking it all back.

00:19:33.815 --> 00:19:38.695
Oh, no, my ATM Card...
My-my secret pin number, 1077.

00:19:38.779 --> 00:19:41.114
I've got nothing left.

00:19:41.198 --> 00:19:42.658
Except...

00:19:45.911 --> 00:19:49.498
You're Fry's relative.
Do you have any idea how he got so crazy?

00:19:49.581 --> 00:19:50.624
Uh, what?

00:19:50.707 --> 00:19:53.752
Oh, yeah, they say madness
runs in our family.

00:19:53.835 --> 00:19:56.296
Some even call me mad.

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:57.464
And why?

00:19:57.547 --> 00:20:01.468
Because I dared to dream
of my own race of atomic monsters.

00:20:01.551 --> 00:20:04.554
Atomic supermen
with octagonal-shaped bodies

00:20:04.638 --> 00:20:06.348
that suck blood out of you...

00:20:06.431 --> 00:20:08.850
Leela, Bender! I missed you so much.

00:20:08.934 --> 00:20:10.644
You did? What happened?

00:20:10.727 --> 00:20:14.147
I was robbed.
They got everything, except these.

00:20:14.231 --> 00:20:15.482
Who did?

00:20:15.565 --> 00:20:17.150
Hello, Fry.

00:20:17.234 --> 00:20:18.652
It's Mom.

00:20:18.735 --> 00:20:22.155
I felt terrible when I heard
about your money troubles

00:20:22.239 --> 00:20:25.200
and I thought maybe I could help out
a sweet young man

00:20:25.284 --> 00:20:27.160
by buying his anchovies.

00:20:27.244 --> 00:20:29.663
Sorry, but the anchovies aren't for sale.

00:20:29.746 --> 00:20:31.999
What? Listen, you little bastard.

00:20:32.082 --> 00:20:35.836
I control the robot oil business
and I won't let you ruin me.

00:20:35.919 --> 00:20:37.337
How much do you want?

00:20:37.421 --> 00:20:39.506
You might as well put that checkbook away

00:20:39.589 --> 00:20:42.342
because I've discovered something
even more important...

00:20:42.426 --> 00:20:45.095
My friends, and they aren't worth
even a penny to me.

00:20:46.054 --> 00:20:48.682
That's why these anchovies
are going on a pizza...

00:20:48.765 --> 00:20:52.144
So I can share the food I love
with the people I like.

00:20:52.227 --> 00:20:55.188
Holy hell! You're going to eat them?

00:20:55.272 --> 00:21:00.319
Oh! Well, just make sure you eat them all.
You're a growing boy.

00:21:00.402 --> 00:21:02.154
Toodle-oo!

00:21:02.237 --> 00:21:03.405
Dumb ass.

00:21:03.488 --> 00:21:04.948
What a nice lady.

00:21:10.954 --> 00:21:14.333
Okay, my friends,
get ready for the most delicious

00:21:14.416 --> 00:21:16.793
extinct animal you've ever tasted.

00:21:17.169 --> 00:21:19.087
I don't know. I've had cow.

00:21:23.133 --> 00:21:24.426
- Gross!
- Ick!

00:21:24.509 --> 00:21:25.802
Mm.

00:21:27.471 --> 00:21:30.265
Eh, no one likes them at first,
but they'll grow on you.

00:21:31.099 --> 00:21:34.144
That stench...

00:21:34.227 --> 00:21:36.021
That heavenly stench.

00:21:40.067 --> 00:21:41.068
More.

00:21:41.151 --> 00:21:43.487
There aren't any more,
and there never will be.

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:45.072
More!

00:21:45.155 --> 00:21:46.615
More!

00:21:46.698 --> 00:21:48.492
More!

00:21:48.575 --> 00:21:50.035
More!